# tools/b/banner_room_witness.rish -- a banner that names a shelf names the shelf the file is on.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. A living document's header sometimes names its own shelf in a field of its own --
# `**Register:** active-designing -- siloed; names only our own modules`. That is a claim about
# where the file lives, and files move. When six documents graduated to `foundations/` on
# `20260821.211423` under the design-rooms test, three of them kept a Register line still naming
# `active-designing`, so each told every future reader it lived in a room it had left.
#
# Nothing was broken, which is why nothing caught it: the links resolved, the prose read true, and
# only the one line saying WHERE was wrong. Three consecutive laps found one of these by hand while
# reading the council rota -- single-stranded, growing-a-language, the-marked-value. A lantern that
# fires twice becomes a loom, so the third became this meter rather than a fourth reading.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal.
#   Every `Register` / `Room` / `Shelf` banner whose first word is a shelf this tree files on names
#   a directory the file actually sits inside. Twenty-nine such banners stood at seating, all
#   agreeing, so the gate is zero with no slack.
#   The check REFUSES a banner naming a shelf the file has left, proven on a planted one.
#   The two honest exemptions are proven rather than asserted -- a Two Rooms voice
#   (`**Register:** Checkable`) and a kind-of-piece Status (`**Status:** Counsel`) both pass free.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. That a banner's OTHER claims are current -- a Status may say `Living` on a
# fossil, and this rung says nothing about it. This proves one sentence: where a file says it is,
# and where it is, are the same place.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/b/banner_room_witness.rish

say "banner-room: Language EN -- a header that names its own shelf makes a claim a reader trusts and a move can quietly falsify. This asks where the file says it is, and where it is."
say "banner-room: Style Radiant -- every shelf-naming banner agrees with its directory, a voice or a kind of piece passes free, and the refusal is proven on a planted move."
say "banner-room: Lens TAME -- docs and implementation stay synced; the failure was silent by construction, since only the line saying WHERE was wrong."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/banner_room_scan.sh"]
assert scan.ok else "banner-room: a banner names a shelf the file has left -- repoint it to where the file sits"
say scan.out
assert scan.out contains "banners_drifted=0" else "banner-room: every shelf-naming banner must name the shelf the file is on"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "banner-room: the scan must balance before it is believed"
say "field GREEN -- every banner that names a shelf names the one its file sits on"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/banner_room_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "banner-room: the control must complete"
say control.out
assert control.out contains "drift_refused=yes" else "banner-room: a banner naming a shelf the file has left must be refused"
assert control.out contains "agreeing_free=yes" else "banner-room: a banner naming its own shelf must pass"
assert control.out contains "voice_free=yes" else "banner-room: a Two Rooms register names a voice, never a room, and must pass free"
assert control.out contains "status_free=yes" else "banner-room: a Status names what a piece is, never where it lives, and must pass free"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "banner-room: the control must agree with itself"
say "RED and GREEN paths proven -- a moved banner refused, an agreeing one kept, a voice and a kind left free"

say "GREEN: banner-room -- where a file says it lives and where it lives are the same shelf."
